  "slug": "reflections-in-the-water-full-collection",
  "title": "Reflections in the Water — Full Collection",
  "summary": "Working with AI art is like gazing into a pond: we're unsure what reflection we'll see. This exhibition explores artists' use of AI to represent the natural form and its possibilities.\n\nJust as still water offers a clear reflection and turbulent water a distorted one, AI-generated images can be hyperrealistic or surreal, with flaws and errors creeping in. \"Reflections in the Water\" examines how artists use machine learning to conjure seascapes, marine creatures, and human forms, sometimes revealing grotesque masks and faces that echo early AI errors and our fascination with self-representation. These artists present AI as a tool and a creative partner.\n\nThe focus on nature and the human form aims for an accessible, tangible exhibition. AI offers opportunities for artwork rooted in technology yet addressing human preoccupations. This theme allows for showcasing AI's evolution, from DeepDream's early outputs to the photorealism of GANs. As perfect realism becomes attainable, artists are focusing on individual styles and conceptual depth.\n\nThis exhibition is timely. Water's appearance is changing due to pollution and climate change. Similarly, AI art's potential is shifting as the technology becomes more predictable. The artists offer a snapshot of our evolving relationship with AI, highlighting its formal confusions, textures, and realism.",
